<title>YEMEN: Yemen's Jan/May oil export income hits $390.2 mln.</title>
<headline>Yemen's Jan/May oil export income hits $390.2 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SANAA 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yemen's income from oil exports in the first five months of this year reached $390.2 million compared with full-year 1996 income from oil exports of $958.4 million, an oil ministry statement said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said local consumption for the same period stood at 10.52 million barrels while the government's share of exports hovered around 20.48 million barrels.</p>
<p>The government's share of crude produced in Yemen in 1996 reached 28.76 million barrels for local consumption, while its share for export stood at 47.03 million barrels.</p>
</text>
